      "classification": "confirmed-frozen-source-proof-starts-with-total-instead-of-partial-candidate",
      "finding": "The theorem rules out any partial computable selector f, defined whenever W_e is computable, but the frozen proof begins only with 'any computable function f'. With the established total-versus-partial terminology, that proves a weaker statement. The subsequent g construction remains partial computable even if f(x) diverges.",
